      "type": "string",
      "description": "Identifier of the conversation."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "chat",
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### chats_list

List conversations.

List the conversations, most recently updated first.

The transcripts are left out: this answers what conversations exist, and
returning every message to answer it would be the most expensive call in the
system. Read one with `chats get`.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "query": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Filter by title, identifier, task or routine."
    },
    "kind": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Narrow to one surface: dm, channel, task, run or external.",
      "enum": [
        "dm",
        "channel",
        "task",
        "run",
        "external"
      ]
    },
    "task": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Only conversations attached to this task."
    },
    "routine": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Only conversations attached to this routine."
    },
    "limit": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Maximum number to return. Defaults to 50."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### chats_react

Toggle a reaction on a message.

Leave a mark on one message, or take it back.

Sending the same reaction twice removes it — which is what clicking the same
emoji twice means, and what keeps one actor from stacking three identical
marks on one message.

Who is reacting comes from the identity of the call, never from the payload:
a caller that could name the actor could react as somebody else.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "chat": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Conversation the message belongs to."
    },
    "message": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Message to react to."
    },
    "value": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The reaction, usually an emoji. Sending the same one again removes it."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "chat",
    "message",
    "value",
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### chats_send

Write to a conversation.

Append a message and hand the turn to whoever should answer.

The message is persisted before anything is dispatched, so a runtime that dies
in between loses the answer and not the question. The result says which agent
was chosen and why, and whether a turn actually started — a message stored with
nobody to answer it is a real state, and one worth knowing about rather than
waiting through.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "chat": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Conversation to write to."
    },
    "text": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "What to say. Address a specific agent with @slug."
    },
    "agent": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Answer with this agent regardless of what the text mentions."
    },
    "context": {
      "type": [
        "null",
        "array"
      ],
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "description": "Material attached to the message for the agent to read, kept apart from what the person typed."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "chat",
    "text",
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### chats_stop

Stop the turn running on a conversation.

Ask the agent working on this conversation to stop.

The turn ends where it is: what it had already written is kept, and the
attempt is recorded as interrupted rather than as an error, because somebody
stopping an agent is not the agent failing.

Answering `stopped: false` is not a refusal. A person presses this
when they see an agent working, and by the time the call lands the turn may
have finished on its own.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "chat": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Conversation whose running turn should stop."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "chat",
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### chats_update

Rename a conversation, or change who can read it.

Change a conversation's name or its visibility.

Only what you name changes. There is no way to send a whole conversation back
and have it written, because that would let a rename drop the transcript or
reopen a private thread to the workspace without anybody asking for it.

Visibility has a consequence worth stating: `workspace` makes the
transcript readable by every member, and there is no undo for what somebody has
already read.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "chat": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Conversation to change."
    },
    "title": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "New name. Leave empty to keep the current one."
    },
    "visibility": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "private restricts to the participants; workspace opens it to every member. Leave empty to keep the current one."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "chat",
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

